
# Adlef-Laravel Project Rules and Context

# Framework and Technologies
Use Laravel as the primary framework
Use Tailwind CSS for styling (not Bootstrap)
Use Jquery for JavaScript interactions. Do not use Alpine.js
Use Laravel Mix for asset compilation

# Project Structure
client routes are in client.php
admin routes are in web.php
views are organized by client/admin sections
use blade templates for views
styles are in resources/css/app.css so make sure to check if there any classes can be used

# Coding Standards
Follow PSR-12 coding standards
Use type hints where possible
Use Laravel's built-in authentication
Follow RESTful conventions for APIs

# Database
Use migrations for database changes
Use seeders for initial data
Use Eloquent ORM for database operations
Follow Laravel naming conventions for tables

# Authentication
Separate auth for admin and client sections
Use Laravel's built-in auth scaffolding
Implement email verification
Store user avatars in storage/app/public

# Frontend Guidelines
Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
Avoid inline styles
Use blade components for reusability
Follow mobile-first approach

# Asset Management
Store images in public/assets/images
Store JS in public/assets/js
Store CSS in public/assets/css
Use Laravel Mix for compilation

# Security
Use CSRF protection
Validate all user inputs
Use Laravel's security features
Implement proper authorization

# Routes
Client routes in routes/client.php
Admin routes in routes/web.php
API routes in routes/api.php

# Models
Store models in app/Models
Use proper relationships
Implement proper validation
Use Laravel's model factories for testing

# Controllers
Organize by client/admin namespace
Follow single responsibility principle
Use form requests for validation
Return proper response codes

# Views
Use blade templates
Organize by section (client/admin)
Use layouts and components
Follow BEM naming convention for CSS

# Testing
Write unit tests for models
Write feature tests for controllers
Use factories for test data
Follow TDD when possible